---
// Redvars' single data path: every caller enters through kernel.api into a session, persistence
// asks the authorizer before touching storage, and PostgreSQL row-level security is the backstop.
// Source: redvars/engineering ARCHITECTURE.md, sections 3.3, 4 and 6.
---

<svg class="diagram" viewBox="0 0 760 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="dp-title dp-desc">
  <title id="dp-title">One door to the data</title>
  <desc id="dp-desc">
    Callers such as the gateway, the UI, rules, scripts and the AI assistant enter through
    kernel.api, which authenticates them into a session bound to one identity and one scope.
    Persistence runs every read and write as parameterised SQL, and before touching storage it asks
    the authorizer, which applies roles, compiles record conditions into the WHERE clause and denies
    by default. PostgreSQL holds real tables and applies row-level security as a backstop.
  </desc>
  <defs>
    <marker id="dp-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
      <path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" class="arrow-head-accent"></path>
    </marker>
  </defs>

  <rect class="region" x="168" y="22" width="392" height="252" rx="16"></rect>
  <text class="tag" x="188" y="46">THE KERNEL'S ONE DATA PATH</text>

  <rect class="box" x="20" y="72" width="128" height="96" rx="12"></rect>
  <text class="label" x="36" y="100">Callers</text>
  <text class="sub" x="36" y="122">gateway · UI</text>
  <text class="sub" x="36" y="138">rules · scripts</text>
  <text class="sub" x="36" y="154">AI assistant</text>

  <path class="edge-accent" d="M148 120 L186 120" marker-end="url(#dp-arrow)"></path>

  <rect class="box-accent" x="188" y="72" width="160" height="96" rx="12"></rect>
  <text class="code" x="204" y="100">kernel.api</text>
  <text class="sub" x="204" y="122">a session bound to</text>
  <text class="sub" x="204" y="138">one identity and</text>
  <text class="sub" x="204" y="154">one scope</text>

  <path class="edge-accent" d="M348 120 L378 120" marker-end="url(#dp-arrow)"></path>

  <rect class="box-accent" x="380" y="72" width="160" height="96" rx="12"></rect>
  <text class="label" x="396" y="100">Persistence</text>
  <text class="sub" x="396" y="122">every read and write,</text>
  <text class="sub" x="396" y="138">as parameterised SQL</text>
  <text class="sub" x="396" y="154">never string-built</text>

  <path class="edge-accent" d="M460 168 L460 190" marker-start="url(#dp-arrow)" marker-end="url(#dp-arrow)"></path>
  <text class="sub" x="470" y="184">asks first</text>

  <rect class="box" x="380" y="192" width="160" height="70" rx="12"></rect>
  <text class="label" x="396" y="216">Authorizer</text>
  <text class="sub" x="396" y="236">roles, conditions in</text>
  <text class="sub" x="396" y="252">WHERE, default deny</text>

  <path class="edge-accent" d="M540 120 L578 120" marker-end="url(#dp-arrow)"></path>

  <rect class="box" x="580" y="72" width="160" height="96" rx="12"></rect>
  <text class="label" x="596" y="100">PostgreSQL</text>
  <text class="sub" x="596" y="122">real tables per app</text>
  <text class="sub" x="596" y="138">row-level security</text>
  <text class="sub" x="596" y="154">as the backstop</text>
</svg>
